Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Do not reset preedit on caret geometry updates

A layout update can move the caret when the input method changes its
preedit. Reporting that movement as CHANGE_CAUSE_OTHER tells input
methods such as Stevia to discard the current composition, causing each
character to appear briefly and then disappear.

Keep geometry updates on the input-method change path. Actual external
edits still use gtk_im_context_wayland_reset() to report OTHER.

The regression was source-bisected to the commit below. The later
bf874024b901 moved its notification into after_layout_cb(). A cause-only
correction fixes the introducing commit as well as source-built 4.23.3.

Fixes: 1d83c7a95320 ("gtk/imwayland: Make text-input caret location animatable")

Candidate for GTK4 upstream and Fedora gtk4 dist-git, against 4.23.3.

--- a/gtk/gtkimcontextwayland.c
+++ b/gtk/gtkimcontextwayland.c
@@ -651,8 +651,12 @@
       context_wayland->surface_cursor_rect.height != rect.height)
     {
       context_wayland->surface_cursor_rect = rect;
+      /* Moving the rendered caret (including while displaying preedit) does
+       * not represent an external edit of the surrounding text. Such edits
+       * are reported separately by gtk_im_context_wayland_reset().
+       */
       notify_im_change (GTK_IM_CONTEXT_WAYLAND (context),
-                        ZWP_TEXT_INPUT_V3_CHANGE_CAUSE_OTHER);
+                        ZWP_TEXT_INPUT_V3_CHANGE_CAUSE_INPUT_METHOD);
     }
 }
 
